  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760156,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1942 (NES) - Synopsis\n\nExperience the thrill of aerial combat in *1942* for the Nintendo Entertainment System, Capcom’s breakout hit and the first installment in the acclaimed *194X* series. Set in the Pacific Theater of World War II, this vertically scrolling shooter puts you in the cockpit of an American P-38 fighter plane, tasked with a surprising mission: reach Tokyo and dismantle the Japanese air fleet. \n\nInspired by the pivotal Battle of Midway, *1942* delivers fast-paced, engaging gameplay. Blast through waves of enemy aircraft and fortifications while collecting power-ups to enhance your firepower. A unique \"roll\" feature allows you to evade enemy fire, adding a layer of strategic depth to the action. \n\nOriginally designed with Western audiences in mind, *1942* became a commercial phenomenon, selling over a million copies worldwide. This NES version faithfully recreates the arcade experience, offering a challenging and rewarding journey through the skies of the Pacific. Prepare for intense dogfights and a nostalgic trip back to the golden age of arcade shooters!"
    },
